      "specialAbilities": [
        {
          "name": "Cover",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "The defensive prowess of Ser Adelphel is second to none, allowing him to focus his actions purely on defending himself and his allies in ways that cannot be replicated. When an ally within 35 feet is targeted with a melee or ranged attack, the he may, as an immediate action, step forward to reposition the ally adjacently to him and forcing the enemy to make the attack roll on the Ser Adelphel's armor class instead. He may move as part of this ability, provided his total movement before his next turn does not exceed his speed (his movement provokes attacks of opportunity as normal). Additionally, while using cover, the holy knight adds five to his AC for the attack.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Holiest of Holy",
          "type": "su",
          "description": "Once every 1d2+1 rounds as a standard action, Ser Adelphel releases an holy light upon his enemies within 100-ft. away from himself. Anyone within 30-ft.-radius from the target takes 8d8 points of holy damage unless they make a Fortitude save (DC 29) for half damage.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Holy Bladedance",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "Once every 1d4+1 rounds as a full-round action, Ser Adelphel strikes in a frenzy of blades towards one target within melee range. He attacks seven times with his knightsword, adding 1d6 points of holy damage per strike, with a -5 penalty.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Holy Shield Bash",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "Once every 1d2+1 rounds as a swift action, Ser Adelphel charges at an target within 60 feet from him. He can attempt to bash them over with his shield (+39) dealing 2d6 points of bludgeoning damage and an extra 1d6 points of holy damage. If he successfully hits, the target must make a Fortitude save (DC 36) or be stunned for 1 round.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Ser Adelphel serves in King Thordan's Knights of the Round. This sheet uses the shared knight traits and Ser Adelphel's individual statistics, equipment and abilities."
